Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Data Held in Tabular Form in Attributes [material flow objects]
Plant Simulation does not save the data of most of the attributes of data type table in a full-fledged table
internally.
If you get the value of such an attribute, the internally held data is copied to a table and Plant Simulation
returns this table. If you change the returned table, the internal data is not changed! To change the
internal data of the attribute, assign such a table to the attribute. Then the data is copied to the attribute.
This applies, for example, to the lists and tables on the tab Exit of the material flow objects, to the tabs
Exit Strategy and Entry Strategy of the FlowControl and to a number of other tables, which you can open
by clicking the button Open List/Open Table.
Example
var t:table[string,string,integer] 
t := MyStation.ExitStrategyMUAttributeList
t.appendRow("Name", "A", 1)                 // the internal data remains 
unchanged
MyStation.ExitStrategyMUAttributeList := t  // writes data back to table
