CreateIn3D [SimTalk]
Sets if Plant Simulation creates the object designated by <Path> in 3D (true) or not (false) .
Remarks
By default, we activated this feature for all simulation-relevant objects, such as the material flow objects,
the fluid objects, the moving objects, the resource objects, and the tools.
When you then insert an instance of this object into the 3D Scene, it shows the icon of the object.
Note
If you deactivate the attribute for an object class and reactivate it again, Plant Simulation restores the
built-in state of the object. It discards all changes which you made in the class of the 3D simulation
object.
Note
If the attribute CreateIn3D has the value false in the origin of an object, then the attribute CreateIn3D
also has the value false in the object itself and cannot be set to true.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.CreateIn3D:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyStation.CreateIn3D := true
See also
Show Non-Simulation-Relevant Objects
CreateIn3D [SimTalk]
