Name [SimTalk] - general description
Sets the name of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The name has to be unique within the name space of the Frame.
You can specify a combination of letters, digits, and underscore (_) characters, for example MyStation,
MyStation1, or My_Station_1.
The name of an object cannot start with a digit, i.e., you cannot specify 1Station.
Note
You cannot change the name of the objects EventController and Connector.
Note
After renaming the object, you can only address it with the new name.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Name:string
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
Example
print MyStation.Name
Station1.name := "shaft"
