AvailableCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Method whenever the state of the Exporter or the Worker designated by <Path>
changes to available.
Within the control you can use the anonymous identifier ? to access the object that triggered the method.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.AvailableCtrl:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
MyExporter.AvailableCtrl := &myAvailableCtrl
See also
Available Control [Exporter]
AvailableCtrl [SimTalk]
11-760 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

ChangePathCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation executes the Change Path Control:
• When the name of the Folder or the Frame designated by <Path> changes. The control is called for all
objects contained in the Folder or Frame. The anonymous identifier @ points to the renamed object.
• When you move the Folder or the Frame designated by <Path>. The control is called for all objects
contained in the Folder or Frame.
Within the Method you can access the moved object with the anonymous identifier question mark ?.
Note
Not each Move action actually moves the object. When you move an object from one Frame to
another, Plant Simulation deletes the object from its source Frame and creates a new object in the
target Frame. Specify an empty string "" as the location to interpret this as the top level in the
hierarchy of objects, as the object basis.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ChangePathCtrl:method
Parameters
Plant Simulation passes three parameters to the Method that is called:
• The parameter oldPath of data type string designates the previous location of the object.
• The parameter newPath of data type string designates the new location of the object.
• The parameter manually of data type boolean indicates if you change the path of the object manually
(true) or with a Method (false).
A change path control might look like this:
param oldPath,newPath: string, manually: boolean
print oldPath
ChangePathCtrl [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-761
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

print newPath
print manually
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
ParallelStation.ChangePathCtrl := &myChangePathCtrl
See also
Change Path Control
ChangePathCtrl [SimTalk]
11-762 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

