ConnectCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Method when you connect the object designated by <Path> with another object
with a Connector and when you delete the connection between two objects.
Note
When you insert a Connector, Plant Simulation first calls the Connect Control for the Connector before
calling the Connect Controls for the objects you are connecting.
When you delete a Connector, Plant Simulation first calls the Connect control for the connected objects
before calling the Destructor Control.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ConnectCtrl:method
Parameters
The method has to define three parameters:
• The parameter predecessor of data type object designates the source object where the connection
starts.
• The parameter successor of data type object designates the destination object where the connection
ends.
• The parameter connector of data type object indicates if the connection is going to be created or
deleted. If the Connector is going to be created, it is assigned to the parameter. If the Connector is going
to be deleted, VOID is assigned.
Example
param ConnectionStart, ConnectionEnd: object, 
ConnectionEstablishedDeleted: boolean
if ConnectionEstablishedDeleted
   print "New"
else
   print "Deleted"
end
ConnectCtrl [SimTalk]
11-764 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

   print "from:",ConnectionStart," to:",ConnectionEnd
end
Note
If you externally connect an Interface of a Frame, the Interface is passed to the parameter predecessor/
successor.
The standard connect control as a user-defined attribute looks like this:
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
MyStation.ConnectCtrl := &myConnectCtrl
See also
Connect Control
Destructor Control
ConnectCtrl [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-765
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

ConstructorCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
