Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

MoveInFrameCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Method when the object designated by <Path> actually changes the position in
the Frame into which you inserted it, meaning that it is moved within its Frame.
Within the control you can access the moved object with the anonymous identifier question mark ?.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.MoveInFrameCtrl:method
Parameters
Plant Simulation passes two parameters to the Method that is called:
• The parameter old is an array of data type length with three parameters. They designate the x-
coordinate, the y-coordinate, and the z-coordinate of the previous position of the object in the Frame.
• The parameter new is an array of data type length with three parameters. They designate the x-
coordinate, the y-coordinate, and the z-coordinate of the new position of the object in the Frame.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Examples
MyStation.MoveInFrameCtrl := &myMoveInFrameCtrl
param old, new: length[3]
print "xv:",previous[1]," yv:",previous[2]," zv:",previous[3], 
"xn:",new[1]," yn:",new[2]," zn:",new[3]
See also
Move in Frame Control
MoveInFrameCtrl [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-775
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

