OpenCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation does not open the dialog of the object though, but calls and runs the source code of the
Open Control. Opening the dialog box is now completely controlled by the source code you specified.
Note
If Plant Simulation cannot open the dialog of the object any longer because of a faulty Method, create
another Method and open the object from there with the method openDialog.
If you use a user-defined attribute of data type method as the Open Control, and if this Method is
encrypted, you cannot open the respective object any longer. Only the Open Control itself, and any other
Method that has been encrypted with the same password as the Open Control, can open the object.
If you specified an Open Control for a subtable, and if you then try to open this subtable, Plant Simulation
runs the control without opening the subtable. This also applies to tables that are part of the object
Variable. This also applies to an object of data type table which you inserted into a Frame.
To prevent the Open Control from being executed, hold down Alt while double-clicking the icon of the
object. Instead, you can also select the command Open Without Control on the context menu of the
object in the Frame.
When you click the button Open Location 
  or Open Origin 
  on the Home Ribbon Tab, you can hold
down the Alt key while you click the button to prevent the Open Control of the class or of the origin to be
executed respectively.
Note
To prevent the Open Control from being bypassed by holding down the Alt key, you can use an
encrypted user-defined attribute of data type method as the Open Control.
If you want to remove the Open Control, you have to decrypt the Method beforehand. As you cannot
open the object in the regular way, you can accomplish this with one of these procedures:
• Decrypt the model as a whole, this also decrypts all Open Controls.
• Click Stop on Controls on the Debugger ribbon tab and then double-click the object. This opens the
Debugger for the Open Control. Select the menu command Tools > Decrypt.
• Call the method decrypt. You might, for example, specify
Frame5.OnOpen.decrypt("MyPassword123")
OpenCtrl [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-779
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
If you specify a user-defined attribute of data type method which you encrypted, you cannot delete or
rename the attribute any longer. You have to decrypt the Method beforehand.
Note
If you open an object from the Method Debugger window, Plant Simulation will not execute the Open
Control. This applies, for example, when you select Open Object on the context menu, or when you
click Open Location 
  or Open Origin 
 .
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.OpenCtrl:method
Parameters for all Objects Except for DataList and DataTable
You can declare these parameters:
• If you declare the Open Control with the parameter from3D of data type boolean, the value of the
parameter will be set to true, if the object is opened from within a 3D window.
• If you declare the Open Control with the parameter inLockedFolder of data type boolean, the value of
the parameter will be set to true, if the object is located within a locked library or a locked folder. If you
do not declare the parameter, i.e., the Open Control expects none or only one parameter, and if the
object to be opened is located within a locked library or a locked folder, the Open Control will not be
called. Instead, Plant Simulation shows an error message letting you know that you are not allowed to
modify the object.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Examples
MyStation.OpenCtrl := VOID // delete entry
MyParallelStation.OpenCtrl := &myOpenControl
param from3D: boolean
var passwordHash:string := computeSHA1Hash(prompt("Password:"))
if passwordHash = "686483805ac47ca14e03514f7481a7973b401762" 
OpenCtrl [SimTalk]
