PauseCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Method whenever you change the paused state of the object designated by
<Path>, when you either select an entry in the drop-down list Paused/Planned/Unplanned 
  or
you assign another value to the attribute Pause.
When you get the paused state within the Method, it shows the state after the change.
The standard pause control as a user-defined attribute looks like this:
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.PauseCtrl:method
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Duration of data type real sets the length of the pause. If the length of the pause is
unknown, Plant Simulation passes -1. The same happens when the control is called at the end of the
pause.
• The parameter NewValue of data type boolean sets that the control will only be called if the
ShiftCalendar changes the state of the object.
In addition, the object will not be put in the desired state. The Pause Control has to do this. The desired
value is passed in the parameter NewValue.
The part still can be processed in its entirety before the object changes to the state paused.
Within the control you can access the paused object with the anonymous identifier ?.
PauseCtrl [SimTalk]
11-782 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
If the Pause Control has the parameters listed above, then the ShiftCalendar will not automatically
change the state paused. This is useful to complete processing of a part and then pause the shift
manually by setting the attribute Pause of the object to true.
Compare this example:
param Duration: real, NewValue: boolean
if ?.Cont /= void
   wait ?.Cont.RemainingProcTime
end
?.Pause := NewValue
Note
If the Pause Control does not have any parameters, Plant Simulation always calls the Pause Control
when the state paused changes.
If the Pause Control has the parameters listed above, Plant Simulation only calls the Pause Control
when the state paused is changed by the ShiftCalendar. This prevents that the Pause Control calls itself
when the paused state is set manually.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Examples
Transporter.PauseCtrl := &myPauseCtrl
print "Current pause ", current.pause
MyStation.pause := current.pause
var shift := root.ShiftCalendar.GetCurrShift
print "Current shift: ", shift
   
if not current.unplanned 
       
if current.pause
   current.currIcon := "pause"
else
   current.currIcon := "working"
end
PauseCtrl [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-783
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

See also
