PermitDeleteCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Note
The Permit Delete Control only applies to the Frame and to the Folder.
Plant Simulation calls Method for the Frame or the Folder designated by <Path>, when you attempt to
delete the object for which you programmed the control.
• If the method returns false, Plant Simulation does not delete the object.
• If the method returns true, Plant Simulation deletes the object and calls a Destructor Control method,
provided you entered one.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.PermitDeleteCtrl:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
Frame.PermitDeleteCtrl := &myPermitDeleteCtrl
See also
Permit Delete Control
Destructor Control
PermitDeleteCtrl [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-785
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

PlausibilityCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Method when you click OK or Apply in the dialog of the object designated by
<Path> or in the windows of list objects to apply the changes you made there.
At this point in time the control checks if the entries are plausible, or it interprets them.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.PlausibilityCtrl:method
Parameters for Lists and Tables
You can declare these parameters:
• If the Plausibility Control has no parameters, Plant Simulation only calls it, when you close the list or
table after making a change. Plant Simulation also considers loading a file into a table as a change. This
way Plant Simulation can check the entry and display an error message if the entry was wrong.
• If the Plausibility Control has two optional parameters of data type integer, Plant Simulation also calls
the control after you edited a cell.
The parameter ColumnNumber of data type integer designates the column number of the edited cell.
The parameter RowNumber of data type integer designates the row number of the edited cell.
When you close the list or table, which you changed, or when you make any changes in any cell, Plant
Simulation calls the Plausibility Control with the values-1 for the column and -1 for the row.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
MyStation.PlausibilityCtrl := &myPlausibilityCtrl
param column,row: integer
switch column
PlausibilityCtrl [SimTalk]
11-786 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

case 1 
// column-specific action
end
See also
Plausibility Control
PlausibilityCtrl [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-787
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

RelabelCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Method whenever you change the Label 
  of
the object designated by <Path>.
Plant Simulation first calls the control for the relabeled object and then for the inheriting objects.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.RelabelCtrl:method
Parameters
Plant Simulation passes three parameters to the Method that is called:
• The parameter CurrentLabel of data type string designates the current label of the object.
• The parameter NewLabel of data type string designates the new label.
• The parameter ManualRename of data type boolean indicates if the object is relabeled by the user
(true) or by assigning a value to the attribute Label (false).
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
MyStation.RelabelCtrl := void
param CurrentLabel, NewLabel: string, ManualRename: boolean
print currentLabel
print newLabel
print manualRename
RelabelCtrl [SimTalk]
