RenameCtrl [SimTalk]
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Method when you change the Name 
  of the
object designated by <Path>.
Plant Simulation calls the control first for the renamed object and then for the inheriting objects.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.RenameCtrl:method
Parameters
Plant Simulation passes three parameters to the Method that is called:
• The parameter CurrentName of data type string designates the current name of the object.
• The parameter NewName of data type string designates the new name of the object.
• The parameter ManualRename of data type boolean indicates if the object is renamed by the user (true)
or by assigning a value to the attribute Name (false).
Note
Plant Simulation does not call the control when you insert the object into a Frame and then assign it a
different name.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
MyStation.RenameCtrl := &myRenameCtrl
param CurrentName, NewName: string, ManualRename: boolean
print CurrentName
