asString [SimTalk] - user-defined attribute
Returns the value of the user-defined attribute as a string.
Remarks
Having the value as a string is especially useful for user-defined attributes of data type object. If the
user-defined attribute contains a relative path, asString returns the relative path.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.<UserDefinedAttribute>.asString → string
Return Value
The return value has the data type string.
Example
Station5.ObjAttribute := "~.ProdMgr.prodplan" 
var a1 := Station5.ObjAttribute              // 
assigns .Models.Model.ProdMgr.prodplan
var a2 := Station5.&ObjAttribute.asString    // assigns "~.ProdMgr.prodplan"
