DecimalPlaces [SimTalk] - user-defined attribute
Sets the number of decimal places which the specified user-defined attribute of the object designated by
<Path> shows in 3D.
Remarks
The user-defined attribute can show up to 15 decimal places. The default setting -1 shows all existing
places.
Specify a positive value to show the number of decimal places, which you entered, in the Frame.
Note
This setting only applies to the Data Types > real, length, money, weight, time, speed, and
acceleration.
The number of decimal places for the data type time affects values differently than for the data type real.
The value -1 for the data type time means that the default time display format is displayed with four
decimal places. A positive value means that Plant Simulation shows the number of decimal places that you
entered at most.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
Path.<UserDefinedAttribute>.DecimalPlaces:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Example
MyStation.myAttribute.DecimalPlaces := 8
SimTalk
