Rotation [SimTalk] - user-defined attribute
Sets the rotation of the user-defined attribute of the object designated by <Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.<UserDefinedAttribute>.Scale:real/real[4]
Assignment Value
You can specify:
• A number which defines the rotation around the negative z-axis at the position at which you inserted
the object.
• An array with four items, which defines the rotation around the specified axis (values 2 to 4) at the
position at which you inserted the object.
If you get the attribute, Plant Simulation returns an array with four items.
Examples
var a : any := MyStation.myAttribute.Rotation
// returns an array of 4 values
MyStation.myAttribute.Rotation := 30
// rotates the user-defined attribute by 30 degrees
MyStation.myAttribute.Rotation := [45, 0, 1, 0]
// rotates the user-defined attribute by 45 degrees around the Y axis
See also
